[[File:Ava chathead.png|left]]
'''Ava''' is a scientist residing in the secret room of [[Draynor Manor]], at the south-west part behind the hidden door next to the [[Bookcase (Draynor Manor)|bookcase]]. She works as the assistant to [[Professor Oddenstein]], after the incident where [[Ernest]] was [[Ernest the Chicken|accidentally polymorphed]]. As part of her research, she created a [[Ava's device|device]] which retrieves used ammunition and other metal items. However, lacking the required materials to make the device, she enlisted the help of a passing [[Player character|adventurer]] to [[Animal Magnetism|gather its components]]. Afterwards, she rewards the player with an [[Ava's attractor|attractor]]. She returns lost devices for a fee of 999 [[coins]].

Ava can upgrade the attractor to an [[Ava's accumulator|accumulator]] for 75 [[steel arrow]]s, provided the player's [[Ranged]] level is at least 50. The accumulator is automatically given if the player meets its requirements when Animal Magnetism is completed.

She also plays a small role in [[Dragon Slayer II]], where the player enlists her help to locate one of the [[dragon key piece]]s. After giving the player a [[locator orb]], Ava mentions she can upgrade the accumulator even further, provided she manages to obtain something "a bit more undead". Upgrading the accumulator to an [[Ava's assembler|assembler]] requires [[Vorkath's head]] (which can only be obtained by killing [[Vorkath]] after completion of Dragon Slayer II) and 75 [[mithril arrow]]s.

After completing [[Animal Magnetism]] and [[Pandemonium]], Ava can provide the player a [[ballistic attractor schematic]] which can be read to learn how to build a [[ballistic attractor]], a [[boat facility]] that recovers 60% of the cannonballs fired by a player.

She can also upgrade a [[Dizana's quiver]] or [[Blessed Dizana's quiver]] with the ammo-saving effects of an [[Ava's device]], [[Ranging cape]] or a [[Max cape]].

Ava also runs a small shop, [[Ava's Odds and Ends]], once [[Animal Magnetism]] is completed. This is handy if a player needs to quickly buy the 75 steel arrows needed to upgrade the device.

