==Trivia==
* Bob was the first non-player character added to ''[[RuneScape Classic]]''. He can be seen in pre-release screenshots with a different skin tone, as his addition predated the option to change the skin of characters.
* ''"Bob is a crazy racist!"'' according to a [[RuneScript]] code comment accompanying Bob's hysterical outburst towards [[Zanik]] during the [[Death to the Dorgeshuun]] quest.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1345372952750141442|date=2 January 2021|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/106759|archivedate=9 January 2021|quote=The developer's intention, in Death to the Dorgeshuun, was very clearly for Bob to be racist: [https://pbs.twimg.com/media/Equ5aYYXIAADewy?format=png ]}}. This comment was written by [[Mod John A]], the main developer of that quest. After Death to the Dorgeshuun was released in [[2006]], "crazy racist" became one of Bob's defining character traits going forward.
* Prior to the removal of the [[Ent (random event)|Ent random event]] in [[2014]], Bob would repair a player's [[Broken axe]] if they failed to notice the Ent in time.
* The painting inside Bob's Brilliant Axe's may be a reference to {{wp|Bob Ross}}'s "Distant Mountains" painting, as the framing and subject are nearly identical.
* As a child, Bob was sent to the [[Varrock Museum]] by his father, hoping he'd follow the path of academia. The museum instead assigned him to preserve and repair [[Third_age_armour|Third Age Armour]], a skill he picked up rather quickly. In the May 2022 edition of the [[Postbag from the Hedge]], he credits this experience as the reason he is able to repair ancient and exotic armours such as those dropped by the [[Barrows Brothers]].
<!-- in order of release -->
* During the [[2017 Birthday event]], Bob was one of several NPCs to challenge the player with a riddle. His riddle was about the cost of repairing an axe, in reference to his historical role repairing axes for players who failed to notice the [[Ent (random event)|Ent random event]] in time.
* During the [[2018 Christmas event]], Bob gave the player an [[Amulet of duplication]].
* During the [[2019 Halloween event]], Bob told the player about a fight that occurred between two goblin trick-or-treaters outside his shop if asked.
* During the [[20th Anniversary event]], Bob expressed displeasure at having the [[Gnome Child (Realm of Memories)|Gnome Child]] in his store. Initially, he said ''"We don't normally serve its kind in this shop."''{{Efn|This phrase references the practice of denying service to individuals on the basis of race during the {{wp|Jim Crow laws|Jim Crow era}}. The specific phrasing "serve your kind" may have originated in the film ''{{wp|Star Wars (film)|Star Wars}}'' (1977), in which the statement ''"We don't serve your kind here"'' is made towards C-3PO by the bartender of the Mos Eisley cantina.{{CiteGeneral|url=https://scholar.harvard.edu/files/jsinger/files/wd.pdf|title=We don't serve your kind here: public accomodations and the mark of sodom|author=Singer, J. W.|year=2015|publisher=Boston University Law Review|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240629054727/https://scholar.harvard.edu/files/jsinger/files/wd.pdf|archivedate=2024-06-29}} This phrasing has since entered general lexicon as a common reference to racist retailers.}}, before being flattered after the Gnome Child mistook him for [[Robert the Strong]] and deciding ''"Your gnome friend is weird, but he's welcome."''
* During the [[2021 Birthday event]], Bob was one of the [[Lumbridge]] citizens to be [[Bob (2021 Birthday event)|attacked by a monkey]].
* During the [[2023 Birthday event]], Bob fixed the [[Cracked cake tin]].

