==Trivia==
*His examine option states he's a baker from the "North", and according to Mod Ash, he is a reference to a real-life baker from Norths Bakery who would sell pies outside Jagex's offices.{{CiteGeneral|url=https://youtu.be/9KPsC26GSHQ?t=811|title=''Story Time Livestream with Mod Ash, Mod Mark, Ian Gower, Mod Noldor & Mod Wilson'', YouTube, 11 February 2015|accessdatedate=11-02-2015}}
*The [[Golem (Desert Treasure II)|golem]] from [[Desert Treasure II - The Fallen Empire]] has Romily Weaklax as a potential search term, although the player is denied from accessing the data pertaining to him. It is currently unknown as to why this may be the case.
*His unusual name and his examine text saying he is from "[[The North|the North]]" has resulted in many speculating that he is a [[Mahjarrat]] in disguise. His name being a search term at the golem and the [[courier task]] where he requests someone to deliver his pies to "some friends of his up north" who "got a big [[Ritual of Rejuvenation|event]] coming up soon" were both added as nods to this player theory.
* Romily Weaklax has an ancestor, Durant Weaklax, who discovered the secret of preventing pies from spoiling on long journeys.{{CitePostbag|issue=39|quote=However, it is said that the great Durant Weaklax discovered the secret back when our family still lived in colder climes up north.|author=Romily Weaklax|letter=letter 2}}

