==Trivia==
* He is the only leprechaun that runs a farming store.
* When Larry's shop is opened, the cocktail glass quantity increases or decreases by a random number 1–6, depending on if the stock is less than or greater than 600. [[Ironmen]] might have difficulties buying cocktail glasses from his shop as they can't purchase overstocked items.
** Larry's stock for cocktail glasses is shared between regular and ironman accounts. Ironmen wishing to purchase cocktail glasses from Larry can use an alt to reduce the stock rather than waiting for stock to decrease.
* Larry's attire, umbrella, and unusual location could be in reference to the Supertramp album "[[wikipedia:Crisis?_What_Crisis?|Crisis? What Crisis?]]" in which a man sits on a beach chair with an umbrella and cocktail while in an industrial area. Larry's nonchalant pose mirrors that of the album cover, as well as the juxtaposition of bright colours in the otherwise grey and dull [[Trollheim]].
* He leaves during the [[Baby Roc]] and [[Giant Roc]] fights, returning afterwards.
** In an update on [[9 April]] [[2025]], he along with all other [[leprechaun]]s was moved closer to [[herb patch]]es. A tipped over [[deckchair#NPC|deckchair]] was left in his original location, which players could use to note herbs still. This change, along with the other leprechaun changes, was reverted in the following update due to community feedback.

